      <notesStmt>
        <note>This article presents the critical edition of a homily by Germain I of Constantinople, celebrating the deliverance of Constantinople from the Avars (626) and the Saracens (718). The homily is preserved in four manuscripts: Lavra Δ 79 (L¹), Lavra E 190 (L²), Vatopédi 633 (Va), and Halki Schol. 41 (H). The homily emphasizes the miraculous intervention of the Theotokos (Mother of God) in saving Constantinople, and it is linked to the liturgical celebration of the Assumption.</note>
      </notesStmt>
